@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title PUT /api/workspace/v1/messenger/message_reactions/[reaction_uuid]
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "WorkspaceMessageReactionController\nRestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\ncanonical lines + brackets" as DB
queue "Transactional outbox\n+ Typed tasks" as Outbox
participant "Worker scope=message\nexact lease + fencing" as Worker
database "Ready projections\nThe container is tied up ." as Projection
database "The public events repository" as Events
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as Dispatcher
actor "The client . WebSocket" as WS
Client -> API: PUT /api/workspace/v1/messenger/message_reactions/{reaction_uuid}
API -> DB: resolve applicable public placement;\ncheck active membership + generation
API -> DB: update one canonical fact + immutable outbox event
DB --> API: The transaction is recorded
API --> Client: A successful public response
DB ->> Outbox: the event that was recorded
Outbox ->> Worker: immutable reaction_snapshot(outbox_event_uuid)\nwithout coalescing
Worker -> Worker: claim (project_id, canonical_message_uuid)\nlease + fencing
Worker -> Projection: MESSAGE.reactions + reaction_users
Worker -> Events: message_reaction.updated + message.updated\natomically in one. DB transaction with a projection
Events ->> Dispatcher: fixed ready line
Dispatcher ->> WS: I 'm going to send / repeat / reproduce
note over API,Worker
  Topic lock Not used; retry/backoff + DLQ/reaper.
  How to restore placement context For the reaction_uuid It stays.
  The central OPEN-The decision; arbitrary placement It 's forbidden ..
end note
@enduml
